  "findings": [
    "Part B, adopted 15 September 2026, identifies September 2026 entrants for year one in B-4.4. Its year-two and year-three tables identify September 2025 and September 2024 entrants respectively. B-4.1 states 144 EC compulsory plus 36 EC free choice or minor.",
    "The public grid and downloadable diagram assign 6 EC to Mathematics for Algorithms and include Software Engineering and Logic in year two. The transition table supports their return as second-year courses from 2027–2028 but gives Mathematics for Algorithms as 5 EC. It supplies no complete upper-year examination programme for the September 2026 cohort.",
    "The public year-three grid shows 30 EC free choice plus compulsory Robots that Learn at 6 EC. The 2026–2027 guide is scoped to current offerings and cannot certify that later requirement. Autonomous Mobile Robots (5082AUMR6Y) is a separate recommended elective in Part B B-4.5. Its current course description does not verify the status or contents of Robots that Learn.",
    "B-4.8 requires completion of years one and two before starting the graduation project. The official project entry supports retaining that gate. It cannot identify the outstanding cohort-specific year-two units.",
    "The second attempt supports the existing partial 156 EC external curriculum and the three separately labelled provisional UCR schedules. The interest, feasibility and content findings remain reusable. Academic and presentation approval remain blocked."
  ],
